Fix a real toolchain-compatibility bug (not an AXOS feature, and unrelated to
RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD): rc/rc.c defines a plain, global getPid_fromFile(),
and the prebuilt rc/prebuild/GT-AX6000/frs_service.o — unconditionally
linked into `rc` (see rc/Makefile: unguarded `OBJS += frs_service.o` and an
unconditional `ifneq ($(wildcard ./prebuild/frs_service.o),)` copy-override
rule) — already defines its own global getPid_fromFile() too. Two
non-static definitions of the same function is a hard "multiple definition"
link error under this cross-toolchain (GCC 9.2/binutils 2.32); this would
happen for ANY GT-AX6000 build of this Merlin release with this toolchain,
regardless of hostapd or any of the other flags touched by earlier patches
in this series — it just happens to be the next thing this build reaches.

Confirmed via a real build attempt: `make gt-ax6000` fails linking `rc` with
"multiple definition of `getPid_fromFile'; rc.o:.../rc.c:95: first defined
here" against frs_service.o's copy.

Fix: make rc.c's own copy `static`. Confirmed via `grep` that nothing outside
rc.c calls getPid_fromFile() (rc.h's extern declaration was otherwise
unused), so giving it internal linkage doesn't change behavior anywhere —
it just stops rc.c's copy from colliding with the prebuilt binary's. The
prebuilt frs_service.o itself is untouched.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0006. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/rc.c b/release/src/router/rc/rc.c
index afdc21d58e..c1358a7531 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/rc.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/rc.c
@@ -91,7 +91,9 @@ double wl_get_txpwr_target_max(char *name);
 double get_wifi_maxpower(int target_unit);
 #endif
 
-int getPid_fromFile(char *file_name)
+/* static: see the comment above rc.h's (removed) extern declaration of this
+ * function — the prebuilt frs_service.o already provides a global copy. */
+static int getPid_fromFile(char *file_name)
 {
 	FILE *fp;
 	char *pidfile = file_name;
diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/rc.h b/release/src/router/rc/rc.h
index 655d5a9f72..92404efd6b 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/rc.h
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/rc.h
@@ -2626,7 +2626,13 @@ extern void stop_dsl_autodet(void);
 extern void stop_dsl_diag(void);
 extern int start_dsl_diag(void);
 #endif
-extern int getPid_fromFile(char *file_name);
+/* Not declared extern here: rc/rc.c's own copy of getPid_fromFile() is
+ * `static` (see rc.c) since the prebuilt rc/prebuild/GT-AX6000/frs_service.o
+ * — unconditionally linked into rc, see rc/Makefile — already defines a
+ * global getPid_fromFile() of its own. Two non-static definitions of the
+ * same symbol is a hard "multiple definition" link error under this
+ * toolchain; only rc.c calls its own copy, so giving it internal linkage
+ * avoids the clash without touching the prebuilt binary. */
 #ifdef RTCONFIG_FRS_LIVE_UPDATE
 extern int firmware_check_update_main(int argc, char *argv[]);
 #endif
